eft and prunes on the budget, on the largest coverages, and on a greedy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"2-packing (vertices with no dominator in common, each needing its own; on trees the largest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"2-packing is γ, Meir and Moon 1975). γ comes from a greedy descent and decisions one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smaller; the least set of γ vertices is then decided vertex by vertex in index order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"against a witness, each decision searching only the part of the problem the vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"touches. Sparse components keep O(n + m) words of state; dense ones (mean degree d with d²","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"above c ⌈c \/ 64⌉) use bitset closed neighbourhoods, under 2m words. Exponential in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component size in the worst case.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the smallest such sets it is the lexicographically least by vertex index (the rule of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges do not matter; isolated vertices are in it."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE20minimumDominatingSetSay6VertexQzGyF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumDominatingSet"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdenti